.TH FSTAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fstat \- obtain metadata for an open file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.BI "int fstat(int " descriptor ", struct stat* " buffer ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR fstat ()
stores metadata for the open file identified by
.I descriptor
in the writable
.I buffer .
It works after the file is renamed or unlinked, as long as the descriptor
remains open.
The target\-specific structure layout is described in
.BR stat (3crunch).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged; \-1 on failure with
.B errno
set to the positive Linux error number.
.SH ERRORS
Possible errors include
.B EBADF
for an invalid descriptor and
.B EFAULT
for an invalid buffer. Other Linux
.BR fstat (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stat (3crunch),
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR fstat (2)
